From 19c4ec4ba7a78a2dc779788697579d7adb739ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:23:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: thread stacks lined up with the PS4's 16 KiB pages for
 fastmem; code caches 48/40/32/8

The PS4's fastmem arena maps 16 KiB at a time, each from 16 KiB of the DRAM, so guest pages must
sit back to back there at their places in a 16 KiB page. A game's thread stacks are heap memory it
aliases (svcMapMemory) at addresses it picks to 4 KiB: mostly not lined up, so every stack access
declined fastmem and walked the page table.

- KPageTableBase::MapMemory (PS4, and EDEN_TEST_ARENA_LINE_UP desktop builds): an alias of heap
  memory up to 8 MiB goes on a copy of the source (CopyAliasForArena): whole 16 KiB from
  AllocateAndOpenContinuous (the applet pool, at most 128 MiB: the application pool is all the
  game's), the alias at its place in a 16 KiB page, the rest of its first and
  last 16 KiB spare pages that become the arena's padding where their guest pages are free
  (FinishAliasCopy). The source keeps its own pages, locked; UnmapMemory copies the alias's data
  back to them (CopyBackAlias, in place of IsValidPageGroup) and frees the copy and its padding
  (ForgetAliasCopy). Skipped when the source lines up already with nothing free beside the alias.
- MapPages: a kernel-allocated stack of whole 16 KiB at a 16 KiB boundary; AllocateAndMapPagesImpl:
  16 KiB-aligned mappings of whole 16 KiB up to 8 MiB on one piece of memory.
- orbis_memory: arena padding (AddArenaPadding, RemoveArenaPadding, PopArenaPadding): a fixed
  table the fault handler reads under arena_lock; ArenaPageSource takes a free guest page there as
  its spare page.
- dynarmic: proactive stack walks only after 32 stack declines on a core.
- Code caches 48, 40, 32, 8 MiB.
- dynarmic x64: DYNARMIC_HOST_FEATURES_MASK (hex) limits the host features, to measure on a desktop
  the code the PS4's Jaguar gets.
- PS4Perf: aliases, aliases_moved, aliases_not_moved, kernel_timer_tasks; per-service queue time
  (request_queue_ns, ServiceCall::queue_ns).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7Cki1YqWbFL1ncEV7C
