+/// Arena padding: the free guest pages beside a stack the kernel lined up with the PS4's 16 KiB
+/// pages (core/hle/kernel: a stack the game maps with svcMapMemory gets memory at the same place in
+/// a 16 KiB page as its address, with spare pages for the rest of its first and last 16 KiB). The
+/// arena maps such a 16 KiB page whole: its guest pages from the page table, its free ones (bit i
+/// of `mask`: the i-th 4 KiB) from the spare pages, which an access there (past the stack's ends,
+/// where the Switch would fault) reads and writes. The 16 KiB at `group_va` is at `dram_offset` in
+/// the DRAM. False if the table is full or has that 16 KiB already (the pages stay the caller's).
+bool AddArenaPadding(std::uint64_t group_va, unsigned mask, std::size_t dram_offset);
+/// Takes the padding of the 16 KiB at `group_va` out of the arena: its mask (0 if none) and DRAM
+/// offset, for the caller to free the spare pages
+unsigned RemoveArenaPadding(std::uint64_t group_va, std::size_t& dram_offset);
+/// Takes any padding out of the arena (the process ends): its mask (0 when there's none left)
+unsigned PopArenaPadding(std::uint64_t& group_va, std::size_t& dram_offset);
+/// The 16 KiB pages with padding now, and how many 16 KiB pages it has let the arena map
+std::size_t ArenaPaddingCount();
+std::size_t ArenaPaddedMaps();
+
 /// RAII: the arena locked while the page table changes (fastmem only)
 class ArenaUpdate {
 public:
